#
# foSSH file contexts. Applied with `restorecon -Rv /usr/bin/fossh-cgi
# /var/lib/fossh /run/fossh` (or a fresh `restorecon -R /` picks these
# up too) after `semodule -i fossh.pp`. The RPM's %post (chapter §3.11)
# runs this automatically — see packaging/rpm/fossh.spec.
#
# Literal `user:role:type:level` contexts, not the `gen_context(...)`
# M4 macro fossh.te's own header explains this module deliberately
# avoids depending on (no selinux-policy-devel M4 library assumed
# available). `checkmodule`/`semodule_package` never validate .fc
# syntax at build time — only bundle it — so an unexpanded
# `gen_context(...)` call here compiled and packaged "successfully"
# every time, and only a real `semodule -i` on a target system ever
# actually parsed it, failing with "Invalid syntax / Bad context / Bad
# filecon declaration". Found by this project's first real clean-VM
# install verification. Expansion confirmed against this machine's own
# real, live /etc/selinux/targeted/contexts/files/file_contexts
# entries (e.g. `/usr/bin/gpg -- system_u:object_r:gpg_exec_t:s0`),
# not assumed from the macro's documented behavior alone.
/usr/bin/fossh-cgi		--	system_u:object_r:fossh_cgi_exec_t:s0
/usr/bin/fossh-fcgi		--	system_u:object_r:fossh_fcgi_exec_t:s0

/var/lib/fossh(/.*)?			system_u:object_r:fossh_data_t:s0

/run/fossh(/.*)?			system_u:object_r:fossh_var_run_t:s0
